# Historical planning files contain installation-specific context and are not
# part of the client product. `git archive` honors export-ignore.
/docs export-ignore
/AGENTS.md export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore

# A checkout on Windows Git (core.autocrlf=true) wrote CRLF into setup.sh, and
# bash inside WSL2 then failed at the shebang with "cannot execute: required
# file not found" (exit 127). Text files are LF on every platform so a clone
# made on the Windows side and copied into WSL2 still runs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Auto-detection is reliable for files holding NUL bytes, but an explicit
# block removes the class of risk entirely and states the intent for the next
# asset type somebody adds.
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
